From e3695d038c32e602e68b09b0445353c71fe1fbb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:47:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/215] fix: ray traced hits get a real specular response (F0
 was quantised to zero)

RT_ProcessBestHit packed the hit reflectance with PackRGB, which is 3 bits per
channel (RT_RGB_RANGE 8). CE's dielectric F0 is MatSpecColor averaged - 0.0369
for a plain material, a hard coded 0.02 for terrain - and round(0.0369 * 7) = 0,
so every non-metal hit arrived at ShadePS with F0 exactly 0. shadeLib.cfi
SpecularBRDF then derives f90 = saturate(dot(f0, 1/3) / 0.02) = 0 and returns
fresnel * spec = 0: no sun highlight, no local light highlight, at every
dielectric hit in every reflection. Only F0 >= 0.0714 survived the first step.

New packing, exact integers in both directions:

  HITPOS.w (RGBA32F, 24 bit mantissa)
      ((hueCode * 256) + greyIdx) * 256 + smoothIdx,  max 14155775 < 2^24
      smoothIdx  8 bit linear        smoothness = smoothIdx / 255
      greyIdx    8 bit SQUARE law    F0max      = (greyIdx / 255)^2
      hueCode    PackRGB base 6      F0         = F0max * hue (hue.max == 1)
      The square law puts 49 of its 256 steps below F0 0.04, so a dielectric now
      round trips to about 0.05 % (0.0369 -> 0.03692) instead of to zero, and a
      coloured metal keeps its tint to ~2.6 bits per channel.

  ALD.w (RGBA16F, integers exact to 2048)
      +-(PackRGB(emissive hue) + 1). The emissive hue moved here to free the
      whole HITPOS.w mantissa; the +1 keeps the lane non zero so the veg leaves
      sign can never be lost - which is how the old encoding lost it, hanging
      the sign on a reflectance code that was 0 for every dielectric.

Sentinels unchanged: RAYDIR.w > 0 is still "this is an RT pixel", ALD.w's sign
is still the transmittance lighting model, HITPOS.w's sign is still reserved for
stage 4 refraction.

SRTInfo: normal_reflectance -> normal_emissive (.w is the ALD.w lane now), new
float3 reflectance holding the linear per channel F0, emissiveTintPacked folded
into normal_emissive.w.

Debug view 12 now packs and unpacks before displaying, so it shows what ShadePS
will actually read; black finally means "the material record has no reflectance"
rather than "the encoding ate it".

Also documents, at the site, the smoothness ground truth: matInfo1.z is exactly
MatSpecColor.w, and the atlas normal alpha is a constant 1 for every _ddna
because CRenderer::DXTDecompress sets sourceChannels = 2 for BC5U and
DXTDecompressRow writes 255 into the alpha byte. The hit gets the material's
smoothness scalar and no smoothness map; that gap is CPU side and is left
visible rather than papered over.

Validated with scene-notes/rt/tools/rtharness2: ShadePS, ConeTracePS, DemosaicPS
and UpScalePS in four flag sets plus BuildRayTracingLightListCS - 17 compiles,
0 errors. Shader only: no C++ change, no new permutation bit, RunTime.ext
untouched.

